there","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3168798641/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3194816680","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109435#issuecomment-3194816680","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109435","id":3194816680,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-bQio","user":{"login":"naturally-intelligent","id":6783606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODM2MDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6783606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent","html_url":"https://github.com/naturally-intelligent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T01:16:07Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T01:16:07Z","body":"AnimationPlayer changing texture **does** work as an alternative!\n\nI tried making independent AnimatedTexture resources but even that wouldnt take, it seems even using the same textures in the animation is enough to keep them tied together somehow.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3194816680/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3565133536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109435#issuecomment-3565133536","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109435","id":3565133536,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Uf57g","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T00:41:13Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T00:41:13Z","body":"`resource_local_to_scene` means local to **scene**, not local to **node**. However, you can save a single node as a scene. You can try **Save Branch as Scene...** on the `Line2D` nodes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3565133536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3568440769","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109435#issuecomment-3568440769","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109435","id":3568440769,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UshXB","user":{"login":"naturally-intelligent","id":6783606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODM2MDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6783606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent","html_url":"https://github.com/naturally-intelligent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-23T23:08:25Z","updated_at":"2025-11-23T23:11:02Z","body":"> `resource_local_to_scene` means local to **scene**, not local to **node**. However, you can save a single node as a scene. You can try **Save Branch as Scene...** on the `Line2D` nodes.\n\nSaving the Line2Ds as separate scenes has no effect\n\nAlso I am pretty sure you are incorrect about your understanding of resource_local_to_scene. Just because the name says scene doesn't mean it behaves that way","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3568440769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3568456422","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109435#issuecomment-3568456422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109435","id":3568456422,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UslLm","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-23T23:25:35Z","updated_at":"2025-11-23T23:36:43Z","body":"> Also I am pretty sure you are incorrect about your understanding of resource_local_to_scene. Just because the name says scene doesn't mean it behaves that way\n\nIt is a **external** resource, and `resource_local_to_scene` limits the scope of its sharing (each scene instance will share one resource instance. Here, the sub-scene root belongs to the sub-scene scope.). Not enabling `resource_local_to_scene` means that it is shared across the entire project (there is **only** one resource instance across the entire project).  \n\nCurrently, `resource_local_to_scene` has not been optimized. It still generates a large number of records in tscn file, and copying scene instances does not take effect immediately; you still need to restart the editor.\n\nIt seems to be another bug that it's not working, possibly because this type resource doesn't take into account situations where `resource_local_to_scene` is enabled.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3568456422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3571425385","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109435#issuecomment-3571425385","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109435","id":3571425385,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U36Bp","user":{"login":"naturally-intelligent","id":6783606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODM2MDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6783606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent","html_url":"https://github.com/naturally-intelligent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T15:35:16Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T15:12:30Z","body":"If you were to check resource_local_to_scene on three node's resources in the same scene, they wouldn't become shared to that scene. It just means that the resource is duplicated/unique three times instead of shared globally.\n\nI think there is confusion because \"scene\" can mean a .tscn file, or \"scene\" can mean a node with its children, depending on the POV.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3571425385/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573567817","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109435#issuecomment-3573567817","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109435","id":3573567817,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VAFFJ","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T02:47:51Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T02:58:54Z","body":"> If you were to check resource_local_to_scene on three node's resources in the same scene, they wouldn't become shared to that scene. It just means that the resource is duplicated/unique instead of shared.\n\nIdeally, it should offer as **few** features as possible, but allow for as **many** combinations as possible. In short, this is reuse. Logic reuse, code reuse, to reduce maintenance costs.\n\nMore basic features:\n1. Enable `resource_local_to_scene` to allow resource instances to be shared within a scene;\n2. Allow single-node scenes;\n\nThese two features enable resource instances to be dedicated to a single node.\n\nFor you, isn't resource sharing within a scene a necessary feature? How can it be implemented? How should it be named?\n\n> I think there is confusion because \"scene\" can mean a .tscn file, or \"scene\" can mean a node with its children, depending on the POV.\n\nThese two are not confused here. They are simply two manifestations of the same mechanism. \n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573567817/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3581781684","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109435#issuecomment-3581781684","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109435","id":3581781684,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Vfaa0","user":{"login":"naturally-intelligent","id":6783606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODM2MDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6783606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent","html_url":"https://github.com/naturally-intelligent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naturally-intelligent/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T15:14:40Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T15:14:40Z","body":"It would make more sense to call the flag \"make_resource_unique\" or something, I think the current name is maybe a leftover from earlier naming conventions.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3581781684/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]